                    "text_key_concerns": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "name": "t:names.text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<h3>There's A Reason Ours Costs More</h3><p>If you’ve seen cheaper “pure titanium” pans online, or even been tricked by one — it’s not your fault. Most use industrial steel alloys with just enough titanium (if any) to slap the name on it. It’s cheaper to produce, but offers none of the benefits, and introduces new risks.</p><p>Taima® is the original, and the only pan made from certified 99.86% pure Grade 1 titanium. Pure titanium is very challenging & expensive to work with. But that’s why it works. And why we’re the only ones who back it with proof.</p><h3>How Does SlipScale™ Work?</h3><p>This technology is the very first of its kind, setting a new standard in cookware. SlipScale™ is our engineered, no-coating imprinted surface pattern that increases food release by up to 3×. The micro-ridges minimize contact points and help distribute oil evenly inside, creating a layer between the food and the pan, so food glides off, not sticks.</p><h3>How Does It Retain More Nutrients?</h3><p>Pure Titanium’s superior thermal conductivity allows you to cook evenly at lower temperatures. Studies show that lower-temp cooking helps retain up to 30% more nutrients (especially vitamin C) in your food compared to traditional cookware.</p><h3>What Is Biocompatibility?</h3><p>Titanium is the most biocompatible metal on Earth — meaning it’s the only metal your body doesn’t react negatively to. That’s why it’s trusted in surgical implants. It’s stable, non-reactive, and perfectly safe for daily contact with food.</p><h3>Why Do Acidic Foods Cause Problems In Other Pans?</h3><p>Acids from pepper, lemon or tomato can react with steel or non-stick coatings, breaking them down and causing heavy metals or chemicals to leach into your food. Titanium is the most corrosion-resistant metal on Earth, so it stays completely stable, no matter what you’re cooking.</p><h3>Is It Pure?</h3><p>SGS is the world’s leading lab for product testing. Our pan is tested to verify its purity (99.86% titanium - Grade 1), the purest possible form.</p><h3>What Does FDA-Compliant Mean?</h3><p>It means the pan meets the FDA’s strict standards for safe food contact — no harmful coatings, metals or chemicals near your meals, lead-free.</p>",
